#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD2265 expect=noViolation domain=TS
#note "Both PCLAS rows pair TSVALCD and TSVAL from the same dummy MED-RT record (N0000000181=Cyclooxygenase Inhibitors, N0000175553=Adrenergic beta-Antagonists), in the preferred case that the flag-less rule compares verbatim (D-TA-3 default, Fix #266; since the C1 data repair the pairs decodes carry the levels' preferred form, so the same TSVAL satisfies the membership twin FDA-SD2263 as well); blank-code and blank-term rows do not fire (completeness is another rule's concern) and the mismatched pair on the AGEMAX row is outside the PCLAS condition -> no violation."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#dictionaries dummy
dataset TS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col TSSEQ    type=Num
col TSPARMCD type=Char
col TSVAL    type=Char
col TSVALCD  type=Char
---
S01 | TS | 1 | PCLAS  | Cyclooxygenase Inhibitors   | N0000000181
S01 | TS | 2 | PCLAS  | Adrenergic beta-Antagonists | N0000175553
S01 | TS | 3 | PCLAS  | Cyclooxygenase Inhibitors   |
S01 | TS | 4 | PCLAS  |                             | N0000000181
S01 | TS | 5 | AGEMAX | Cyclooxygenase Inhibitors   | N0000175553
